{"id":"word:hebrew:H6453","type":"word","title":"פֶּסַח","subtitle":"H6453 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a pretermission , i.e. exemption ; used only techically of the Jewish Passover (the festival or the victim)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to פֶּסַח (H6453) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 49 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"פֶּסַח (peçach) means a pretermission , i.e. exemption ; used only techically of the Jewish Passover (the festival or the victim) First listed occurrence: 2Chr 30 1."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"פֶּסַח","transliteration":"peçach","pronunciation":"peh'-sakh","strong":"H6453","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6453","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["הַ/פֶּ֖סַח","הַ/פָּ֑סַח","הַ/פֶּ֔סַח","פֶּ֖סַח","הַ/פָּֽסַח"],"morphs":[["HTd/Ncmsa",29],["HNcmsa",14],["HRd/Ncmpa",3],["HRd/Ncmsa",2],["HTd/Ncmpa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a pretermission , i.e. exemption ; used only techically of the Jewish Passover (the festival or the victim)","usage":"passover (offering).","full":"H6453. pesach מֶּ֫סַח noun masculine passover (usually (Thes and most) from I. פסח , with reference to Exod 12:13 etc.; Reuss Geschichte. AT § 58 passing over into new year; Schaefer Passah-Mazzoth (1900), 346 compare Assyrian pašâ—u , soothe , placate [deity], &lt; be soothed , Pi`el transitive, Jen ZA iv (1889), 275 Zim Babylonian Rel. i (1896). Glossary ; ii (1899), 92; Schw Idiot, 124 from II. פסח , of sacred dance); — absolute ׳פ 12:11 +; מָּ֑סַח 12:21 +; plural מְּסָחִים 2Chr 30:17 3 t.; — 1 sacrifice of Passover , involving communion-meal, hence a species of peace-offering (compare I. זֶבַח II. 2 ), פ ׳זֶבַח לי ׳הוא Exod 12:27 (J), compare 12:11 (P); פ ׳זָבַח Deut 16:2 , 5 , 6 ; הפ ׳אבל 2Chr 30:18 ; the special feature lay in the application of blood to homes to consecrate them: compare simile Babylonian rite of purification Zim ib. ii. 126-7. 2 the animal victim of the passover: פ ׳שׁחט Exod 12:21 (J) 2Chr 30:15 ; 35:1 ; 35:6 ; 35:11 ; Ezra 6:20 , compare 2Chr 30:17 ; הפ ׳בשׁל באשׁ 35:13 ; לפסחים 35:7-8 , 9 . [Passover animals (compare Br Hex.206 ) were צאֹן flock Exod 12:21 (J), שֶׁה 12:3 ; 12:4 ; 12:5 , including כֶּבֶשׁ and עֵז 12:5 (P); ובקר צאן Deut 16:2 ; large numbers of all these ( שֶׂה not used) in Josiah's Passover, active to 2Chr 35:7-8 , 9 , but evident mingling of whole burnt-offerings for the passover with special passover victim.] 3 festival of the passover : הפ ׳חג Exod 34:25 (J); ׳(ה)פ Lev 23:5 ; Num 28:16 ; 33:3 ; Josh 5:11 (P) Ezek 45:21 ; הפ ׳חֻקַּת Exod 12:43 ; Num 9:12 , 14 (P); פ ׳עשׂה Exod 12:48 ; Num 9:2 , 4 , 5 , 6 , 10 , 13 , 14 ; Josh 5:10 (P) Deut 16:1 ; 2Kin 23:21-22 , 23 ; 2Chr 30:1-2 , 5 ; 35:1 , 16 , 17 , 18 (twice in verse); 35:19 ; Ezra 6:19 ; it was held in month הָאָבִיב Deut 16:1 , בָּעָ֑רֶב 16:6 ; on 14th day Josh 5:10 (P), of 1st month Ezek 45:21 ; הערבים בֵּין ( Exod 12:6 ) Lev 23:5 ; Num 9:5 (P); if impossible at that time, then on 14th of 2nd month 9:10 , 12 . [No reference to מֶּסַח in E; J subordinates it to מַצּוֺת (the great feast of J E); in D it predominates over מצות ; P makes it first in importance (Br Hex.195f. )].]","rootNote":"from 6452 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Chr 30 1","keyReferences":["2Chr 30 1","2Chr 30 2","2Chr 30 5","2Chr 30 15","2Chr 30 17","2Chr 30 18","2Chr 35 1","2Chr 35 1"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":49,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Chr 30 1","book":"2Chr","chapter":30,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"פֶּ֔סַח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 30 2","book":"2Chr","chapter":30,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/פֶּ֖סַח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 30 5","book":"2Chr","chapter":30,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"פֶּ֛סַ